# Recorded measurements that are inputs to a result, not text anyone reads.
#
# `-diff` makes git treat them as binary for diffing only: they are still
# tracked, versioned and stored exactly as before, but a diff reports "binary
# files differ" instead of thousands of lines nobody reviews.
# `linguist-generated` is the GitHub half, which collapses them in a pull
# request and keeps them out of its line counts.

# Measured expert routing demand: one number per (layer, expert) pair, 19,200
# of them for GLM-5.2 at 75 layers x 256 experts. Produced by the profiler and
# consumed by the simulator; a human never reads a row of it.
presets/alignment/*/expert_popularity.json -diff linguist-generated=true
